Phase 1: Make backend deploy-ready and able to accept orders (no new features)

Scope: Hardening, configuration, operational readiness, and payment/webhook closure so the current functionality works end-to-end in production.

1) Security & Settings
- [✔] Externalize all secrets via environment variables and NEVER commit real values.
  - [✔] SECRET_KEY: read from env; fail on missing in production (DEBUG=0)
  - [✔] SIMPLE_JWT signing/algorithm settings pinned (optional), tokens lifetimes env-driven
  - [✔] RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY must be set in prod; block login if missing (or disable recaptcha gate explicitly)
  - [✔] TOTP_SECRET set from env (already wired) – generate a strong secret
- [ ] Use Decouple for settings management
- [ ] Move values to constants.py where appropriate (e.g., PAYMENT_MODES)
- [✘] CSRF/CORS
  - [✘] CORS_ALLOW_ALL_ORIGINS is currently True; for prod restrict to FE domain(s) only
  - [✘] Use explicit CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS from env (list of exact origins); remove wildcard logic or ensure it’s safe and covered by tests. Wildcard middleware is permissive – review necessity
- [✘] Allowed Hosts & HTTPS
  - [✘] ALLOWED_HOSTS must include public backend hostname(s)
  - [✘] Configure SECURE_* headers when running behind TLS (e.g., SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER, SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE, CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE, SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS)

2) Database & Migrations
- [✘] Decide DB for production
  - [✘] SQLite is configured; acceptable for very small installs but not for scale or concurrency. Consider Postgres for production
  - [✘] If staying on SQLite, ensure volume persistence (already defined) and backups
- [✘] Run and verify migrations on startup (already in entrypoint). Add health check endpoint or use `python -m django check --deploy` in CI

3) Static/Media
- [✘] Static files collected by entrypoint (OK). Ensure correct storage and caching headers via WhiteNoise
- [✘] MEDIA files served by app container for now (OK for small scale). For larger deploys, plan object storage (S3/Cloud)

4) Authentication & Onboarding
- [✔] Phone-based login flow
  - [✘] recaptcha_verify requires RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY; configure prod key and test
  - [✔] OTP model stores codes; integrate with Fast2SMS for OTP delivery (Phase 1 basic); rate limiting enforced
  - [✔] Ensure `authentication.managers.UserManager` is implemented and migrations created (confirm present)
- [✔] JWT Access
  - [✔] Confirm clock skew tolerance and token lifetimes; rotate refresh tokens (already True)

5) Payments & Order lifecycle
- [✔] Keys in code (critical): move payment gateway keys to environment variables immediately
  - [✔] PhonePe: merchant_id, salt_key, salt_index, env
  - [✔] Razorpay: api_key, api_secret
  - [✔] Paytm: MID, secret, website, env URLs
  - [✔] Remove test keys from VCS and read via env; default to STAGING in DEBUG
- [✔] Callback endpoint `/ecom/callback`
  - [✔] Verify idempotency: updating `Payment` and creating `OrderStatus` ‘Paid’ should be safe on repeated callbacks; ensure not duplicating statuses repeatedly or allow duplicates but harmless
  - [✔] Validate the callback authenticity using provider signatures/hashes before trusting status (best-effort by pulling status from the gateway server-side)
  - [✔] Update `Order.status` string to current status when marking paid (now updated alongside `OrderStatus`)
- [✔] Order placement
  - [✘] On `OrderViewSet.create`, ensure stock check and reservation or at least availability check for `ProductVariant.stock` and decrement upon successful payment or order creation per business rule
  - [✔] Ensure `Cart` address and payment_mode are required prior to checkout (serializer validates address; OK). Validate payment_mode present
  - [✘] Clear cart after order creation (already does). Consider moving to after successful payment for prepaid modes (business decision)
- [✔] Payment method listing
  - [✔] `ecom/utils.PAYMENT_MODES` contains COD + 3 gateways. Ensure disabling unwanted gateways via env feature flags

6) Admin & Ops
- [✘] Create superuser on first boot (optional via env) for quick access
- [✘] Add Django Admin hardening: disable admin if not needed; protect via IP allowlist or admin path change
- [✘] Logging
  - [✘] RotatingFileHandler configured; ensure container logs also go to stdout/stderr; already using Gunicorn logs to stdout. Keep app error logs rotating file
  - [✘] Add request/response logging for payment flows at INFO level without PII

7) API Surface & Docs
- [✘] Ensure minimal API contract documented for FE:
  - [✘] Auth: `/api/auth/login/`, `/api/auth/refresh/`, `/api/auth/send-otp/`
  - [✘] Catalog: `/api/ecom/categories/`, `/api/ecom/products/`, `/api/ecom/category-products/`
  - [✘] Cart: `/api/ecom/cart/` CRUD, `/api/ecom/coupon/`, `/api/ecom/address/`
  - [✘] Checkout: `/api/ecom/orders/` POST to create order; `/api/ecom/orders/{id}/` GET; `/api/ecom/orders/{id}/` PUT to get payment config
  - [✘] Payment: `/api/ecom/payment/` GET list methods; POST select
  - [✘] Callback: `/ecom/callback?pg=...&transaction_id=...`
- [✔] Provide Postman collection or OpenAPI schema (optional via drf-spectacular)

8) Docker/Deploy
- [✔] Dockerfile/compose
  - [✔] Remove bind-mount of entire repo in prod compose; mount only data volume. Rely on built image
  - [✘] Add healthcheck (curl /admin/login/ or /api/)
  - [✘] Configure environment: `DEBUG=0`, `ALLOWED_HOSTS`, `CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`, `FE_SITE`, `BE_SITE`, payment keys
- [✘] Reverse proxy
  - [✘] Put Nginx/Traefik in front to terminate TLS, set headers and handle static if desired
- [✘] Database
  - [✘] If moving to Postgres: add service and env vars; configure `DATABASES` via env

9) Data & Seed
- [✘] Initial admin and sample data script (management command) for categories/products/images/variants so FE has something to show
- [✘] Media upload path exists; verify

10) Testing & Readiness checks
- [✔] Add smoke tests for critical flows (catalog list, login+JWT, add to cart, set address, set payment, create order, update order to get payment config)
- [✘] Run `python manage.py check --deploy` and fix warnings
- [✔] Add rate limits for sensitive endpoints (send-otp, login) via DRF throttling

11) Add Google Analytics

12) others
Callback verification and idempotency: Add signature/hash verification for all callbacks and make updates idempotent.
  Fix order status handling and the malformed f-string in OrderViewSet.update:
  Keep Order.status synchronized or compute from OrderStatus safely.

Env variables to add (example .env):
- DEBUG=0
- SECRET_KEY=your-strong-secret
- ALLOWED_HOSTS=backend.example.com
- CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://frontend.example.com,https://backend.example.com
- FE_SITE=https://frontend.example.com
- BE_SITE=https://backend.example.com
- RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=... (prod key)
- TOTP_SECRET=... (random, strong)
- PHONEPE_MERCHANT_ID=
- PHONEPE_SALT_KEY=
- PHONEPE_SALT_INDEX=1
- PHONEPE_ENV=uat|prod
- RAZORPAY_API_KEY=
- RAZORPAY_API_SECRET=
- PAYTM_MID=
- PAYTM_SECRET=
- PAYTM_WEBSITE=DEFAULT|WEBSTAGING
- PAYTM_ENV_URL=https://securegw.paytm.in|https://securegw-stage.paytm.in
- ENABLE_GATEWAY_PHONEPE=1
- ENABLE_GATEWAY_RAZORPAY=1
- ENABLE_GATEWAY_PAYTM=1

Acceptance criteria for Phase 1 (deploy-ready):
- All secrets and payment keys are loaded from env; no hardcoded credentials remain
- CORS/CSRF/checks scoped to real FE origin; DEBUG=0
- App builds docker image and starts with migrations+collectstatic
- Auth (send-otp, login) returns JWT and recaptcha is enforced
- Catalog endpoints return data; cart and address endpoints work
- Order creation succeeds with Cart set up; payment update returns gateway config and redirects complete to FE callback
- Callbacks update the Payment record and Order status to Paid after signature verification
- Comprehensive smoke test suite validates end-to-end critical flows: ✅ catalog, ✅ auth+JWT, ✅ cart, ✅ address, ✅ payment (methods), checkout (needs investigation)
